-- Vocabulary V4 step by step (IELTS-V4 v1.1.0): five guided steps and one mixed check, in the Lesson 6 format
-- (LEARN FIRST worked example, an explanation for every answer). Auto-marked, so filed as reading tasks; every item is
-- mapped to the vocabulary subskill it practises. Owner instruction 2026-10-28 13:01 (Asia/Bishkek): 'Go next'.
-- Named-student pilot with requires_review; nothing is released. Source: docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json.
do $steps$
declare art constant text := '

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

THE TRANSCRIPT: a Speaking Part 3 discussion about tourism

EXAMINER: Let''s talk about tourism. Do you think tourism has more advantages or disadvantages for a city?

CANDIDATE: That''s a tricky question, but on the whole I''d say the advantages are greater, at least economically. Tourism creates a lot of jobs, not only in hotels but in restaurants, transport and shops. In my home city, for instance, the old market used to be almost empty, and now it''s bustling with visitors for most of the year.

EXAMINER: Why do you think some residents dislike tourists?

CANDIDATE: I suppose it''s mainly about crowding and prices. When an area becomes popular, rents tend to go up, and local people can end up being pushed out of neighbourhoods where their families have lived for generations. So, to be honest, I can understand why they feel frustrated, even if they also benefit from the jobs.

EXAMINER: Would that be true in every city?

CANDIDATE: Probably not. It depends on the size of the city and how the tourism is managed. A large capital can absorb millions of visitors without much difficulty, whereas a small historic town might be completely overwhelmed. What I mean is, the same number of tourists can be a benefit in one place and a burden in another.

EXAMINER: How might tourism change in the future?

CANDIDATE: Looking ahead, I think more cities will limit visitor numbers, perhaps through booking systems or higher taxes on short-term rentals. Then again, cheaper flights could push numbers up even further, so it''s hard to predict. Personally, I''d like to see more people visiting smaller towns rather than the same famous places.';
begin
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r76-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V4 step 1 of 6: What does each phrase do?','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose what each speaking phrase is used for.','Each phrase has a job. Use it for that job, not to fill silence: buy time, soften, balance, rephrase, describe, reflect.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "''That''s a tricky question, but ...''", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  buy thinking time"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  soften an opinion"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  add a balancing point"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  rephrase to be clearer"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  describe a word you cannot remember"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  reflect on the past"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "''What I mean is ...''", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  buy thinking time"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  soften an opinion"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  add a balancing point"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  rephrase to be clearer"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  describe a word you cannot remember"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  reflect on the past"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "''Looking back, ...''", "accepted_answers": ["F"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  buy thinking time"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  soften an opinion"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  add a balancing point"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  rephrase to be clearer"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  describe a word you cannot remember"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  reflect on the past"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "''It''s a kind of small boat used for fishing.''", "accepted_answers": ["E"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  buy thinking time"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  soften an opinion"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  add a balancing point"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  rephrase to be clearer"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  describe a word you cannot remember"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  reflect on the past"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "''I''d say it''s mainly a question of money.''", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  buy thinking time"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  soften an opinion"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  add a balancing point"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  rephrase to be clearer"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  describe a word you cannot remember"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  reflect on the past"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "''Then again, it can be expensive.''", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  buy thinking time"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  soften an opinion"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  add a balancing point"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  rephrase to be clearer"}, {"value": "E", "label": "E  describe a word you cannot remember"}, {"value": "F", "label": "F  reflect on the past"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 6, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 A, buy thinking time: it gives you a moment, honestly, before you answer.\n2 D, rephrase to be clearer: you say the same idea again in a simpler way.\n3 F, reflect on the past: ''Looking back, it was the right decision.''\n4 E, describe a word you cannot remember: you explain the thing instead of stopping.\n5 B, soften an opinion: ''I''d say'' makes the opinion sound natural and less absolute.\n6 C, add a balancing point: it introduces the other side.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Adjust degree of formality: recognise the function of natural spoken phrases."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: speaking phrases have jobs

Natural speakers use short phrases to manage a conversation:
- buy thinking time: That''s a tricky question, but ...
- soften an opinion: I''d say ... / I suppose ...
- add a balancing point: Then again, ... / On the other hand, ...
- rephrase to be clearer: What I mean is ... / To put it another way, ...
- describe a word you cannot remember: It''s a kind of ... / the thing you use to ...
- reflect on the past: Looking back, ...

WORKED EXAMPLE
''On the whole, I enjoy living here.''
''On the whole'' = in general. It gives a balanced overall opinion, not an extreme one.

Now name the job of six phrases.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'15a6222c91ecfc0dcf85a2a66bc3a00d97ff2c154e481c8be6e981abb58a2b83',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r77-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V4 step 2 of 6: Natural describing words','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose the word that completes each sentence naturally.','Some words go together: a bustling market, a breathtaking view, a down-to-earth person, I''d highly recommend, a real eye-opener.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "The view from the top of the mountain was ______.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  down-to-earth"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  breathtaking"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  bustling"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  lively"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "Saturday is the best day to visit the ______ market.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  down-to-earth"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  bustling"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  breathtaking"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  easy-going"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "My aunt is very ______; she never pretends to be something she isn''t.", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  down-to-earth"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  bustling"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  stunning"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  breathtaking"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "I''d ______ recommend the museum café.", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  high"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  much"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  highly"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  very"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Working in a hospital for a week was a real ______; I had no idea how hard nurses work.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  kind of"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  on the whole"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  tricky question"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  eye-opener"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "On the ______, I enjoy living in a small town.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  all"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  complete"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  total"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  whole"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 6, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 B, breathtaking: extremely beautiful, used for views and scenery.\n2 B, bustling: full of busy activity, used for markets and streets.\n3 A, down-to-earth: practical, honest and friendly, used for people.\n4 C, highly: ''I''d highly recommend'' is the natural collocation. ''Very recommend'' is not English.\n5 D, eye-opener: an experience that taught you something surprising.\n6 D, whole: ''on the whole'' = in general.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Choose precise spoken vocabulary: use natural collocations for people, places and experiences."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: words that go together

Examiners notice natural collocations: words that are often used together.
- a bustling / lively market or street = full of busy activity
- a breathtaking / stunning view = extremely beautiful
- a down-to-earth / easy-going person = practical and friendly / relaxed
- I''d highly recommend ... = I strongly suggest
- it was a real eye-opener = it taught me something surprising
- on the whole / by and large = in general

WORKED EXAMPLE
''My uncle is very ______; he''s practical and friendly.''
''Bustling'' describes places, not people. -> down-to-earth

Now choose six words.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'82b289d5413d4f93c472a7d459ba14e6eaa60604d8591f26c660de491ef41ec7',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r78-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V4 step 3 of 6: The best reply','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose the reply that an examiner would reward most: natural, accurate and developed.','The best reply answers the question, gives a reason or example, and sounds natural. Avoid one-word answers, memorised speeches and repetition.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "''Do you enjoy cooking?''", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Yes."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  Cooking is an activity which is enjoyed by many people all around the world."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Yes, I''d say I do, mainly because it helps me relax. I often make soup with my mum at weekends."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  Yes, I like cooking, I like cooking very much, cooking is nice."}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "''Is it better to study in the morning or the evening?'' (Part 3)", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Studying is very important for students and their future careers."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  I study in the morning and the evening and the afternoon."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Morning."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  I suppose it depends on the person. Some people concentrate best early in the day; then again, others feel more awake at night."}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "''Describe a place you would recommend.''", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  I recommend it, I really recommend it, it''s very recommended."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  I''d highly recommend the old market in my city. It''s bustling in the mornings, and you can try local food that you won''t find anywhere else."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  I would like to describe a place which I would recommend to other people."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  The market. It is good."}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "''What do you dislike about your town?''", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  My town is a town in my country with many people."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  Nothing."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Everything is terrible there."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  To be honest, the traffic can be a bit frustrating, especially in the evening when everyone is driving home."}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "''Do you think people read less than in the past?'' (Part 3)", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  On the whole, I''d say yes, at least when it comes to books. Then again, people probably read more short texts on their phones than ever."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  People read less, less than before, much less."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Reading is a very important skill which everybody should have."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  Yes, because of phones. Next question."}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "''Has technology made life easier?'' (Part 3)", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Yes. Technology. Phones."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  In many ways, yes. For instance, I can pay bills in a minute. What I mean is, it saves time, although it can also make us busier."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Technology has made life easier and technology is easier now."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  Technology is good and bad."}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 C, It answers, gives a reason (it helps me relax) and an example (soup at weekends). The others are too short, memorised or repetitive.\n2 D, It shows the answer varies (''it depends on''), explains both sides and balances them (''then again'').\n3 B, It uses natural collocations (highly recommend, bustling) and gives a reason to go.\n4 D, ''To be honest'' introduces a sincere criticism, and the detail (in the evening) develops it. ''Everything is terrible'' is extreme and unsupported.\n5 A, It gives a balanced opinion (on the whole, I''d say), limits it (at least when it comes to books) and adds a balancing point.\n6 B, It answers, gives an example (paying bills), rephrases to make the point clearer (what I mean is) and adds a qualification.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Use a range of spoken vocabulary: choose natural, developed answers over short, memorised or repetitive ones."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: answer, reason, example

A strong spoken answer is natural and developed:
1. ANSWER the question directly.
2. Add a REASON (because, mainly because).
3. Add an EXAMPLE or a detail (for instance, in my case).
Avoid: one-word answers, memorised ''textbook'' sentences, and repeating the same words.

WORKED EXAMPLE
''Do you like the area where you live?''
Too short: ''Yes.''
Memorised: ''My neighbourhood is a place which has many advantages and disadvantages.''
Natural and developed: ''On the whole, yes. It''s quite quiet, but there''s a lively market at the weekend, so there''s always something to do.''

Now choose six replies.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'91ff74fd598cef483dd972af3e54bf5178c3f18ebbc1adb3307d51a4a7ea94bc',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r79-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V4 step 4 of 6: When you get stuck','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then choose what a strong candidate would say in each situation.','Never stop or say ''I don''t know the word''. Describe it, ask for repetition politely, buy time honestly, or rephrase.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "You cannot remember the word ''microwave''.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  It''s a thing."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  It''s a kind of small oven you use to heat food quickly."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  (Say nothing and wait.)"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  I don''t know the word."}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "You did not understand the examiner''s question.", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Sorry, could you repeat the question, please?"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  (Answer a different question.)"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Next question, please."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  What?"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "You need a few seconds to think about a difficult Part 3 question.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Ummmm ... (a long silence)"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  Can we skip this one?"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  I don''t know."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  That''s a tricky question, but I suppose ..."}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "You realise your last sentence was not clear.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Sorry, my English is bad."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  What I mean is, it saves people a lot of time."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  (Repeat the same sentence again.)"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  Forget it."}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "You have given one side and want to show the other side too.", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Then again, it can be quite expensive."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  So that is my answer."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  But no."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  That''s all."}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "You cannot remember the word ''stapler''.", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  stapling"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  I forgot"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  the thing you use to join pieces of paper together"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  a paper"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 6, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 B, Describe it: what kind of thing it is and what you use it for.\n2 A, Ask politely for repetition. In Parts 1 and 3 this is allowed and sounds natural.\n3 D, Buy time honestly with a natural phrase, then start answering.\n4 B, Rephrase to make the point clearer.\n5 A, Add a balancing point with ''then again''.\n6 C, Describe what the thing does: ''the thing you use to ...''.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Choose precise spoken vocabulary: use repair strategies to keep speaking fluently."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: keep going, don''t stop

Everyone forgets a word or needs a moment. Strong candidates keep going:
- Forgot a word: describe it. ''It''s a kind of ...'' / ''the thing you use to ...''
- Did not understand: ''Sorry, could you repeat the question, please?''
- Need time: ''That''s a tricky question, but I suppose ...''
- Not clear: ''What I mean is ...''
Never say ''I don''t know the word'' and stop.

WORKED EXAMPLE
You cannot remember the word ''umbrella''.
''I took one of those things you hold over your head when it rains.''
The examiner understands you, and you keep speaking.

Now choose what to say six times.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'6ef7c099e3026c59eff7dd1548dc4b59209d9e48d047a3a28a7a3e69ee2746ed',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r80-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V4 step 5 of 6: Read a strong answer','reading','guided_practice','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then read the transcript and answer six questions about how the candidate develops her answers.','Notice how each phrase helps her: limiting an opinion, giving an example, showing sympathy, answering directly then explaining.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "In her first answer, ''at least economically'' shows that she ...", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "aafe14e8-c993-48b3-ae4a-2c26b2021897", "supporting_node_id": "e55dff22-7ea2-4bb6-b724-7d129b554bb4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  gives an example from her city"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  limits her opinion to one area"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  strongly disagrees with the examiner"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  changes the topic"}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "''For instance'' introduces ...", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "aafe14e8-c993-48b3-ae4a-2c26b2021897", "supporting_node_id": "e75c01d6-b850-4f9e-87bb-f014b7c3947f", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a question for the examiner"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  an example from her home city"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  a reason for her opinion"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  a balancing point"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "''So, to be honest, I can understand why they feel frustrated'' shows that she ...", "accepted_answers": ["A"], "taxonomy_node_id": "aafe14e8-c993-48b3-ae4a-2c26b2021897", "supporting_node_id": "3cc4beec-8c09-4289-bd3d-185f5319240a", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  sympathises with residents while still seeing the benefits"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  agrees that tourism should stop"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  thinks residents are wrong"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  is frustrated with tourists herself"}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "When the examiner asks ''Would that be true in every city?'', she ...", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "aafe14e8-c993-48b3-ae4a-2c26b2021897", "supporting_node_id": "e75c01d6-b850-4f9e-87bb-f014b7c3947f", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  repeats her first answer"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  asks the examiner to explain"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  gives a short direct answer and then explains it"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  refuses to answer"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "In ''a benefit in one place and a burden in another'', ''burden'' means ...", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "aafe14e8-c993-48b3-ae4a-2c26b2021897", "supporting_node_id": "e55dff22-7ea2-4bb6-b724-7d129b554bb4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a famous attraction"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a benefit"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  something that causes problems or difficulty"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  a large number of visitors"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "''Personally, I''d like to see ...'' is used to ...", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "aafe14e8-c993-48b3-ae4a-2c26b2021897", "supporting_node_id": "3cc4beec-8c09-4289-bd3d-185f5319240a", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  disagree with the examiner"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  report what experts think"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  describe the past"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  give her own preference at the end"}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 8, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 B, limits her opinion to one area: \"on the whole I''d say the advantages are greater, at least economically\". She is not claiming tourism is better in every way.\n2 B, an example: \"In my home city, for instance, the old market used to be almost empty, and now it''s bustling with visitors\".\n3 A, sympathises while still seeing the benefits: she adds \"even if they also benefit from the jobs\".\n4 C, a direct answer then the reason: \"Probably not. It depends on the size of the city and how the tourism is managed.\"\n5 C, something that causes problems: it is the opposite of ''a benefit'' in the same sentence. \"the same number of tourists can be a benefit in one place and a burden in another\".\n6 D, give her own preference: \"Personally, I''d like to see more people visiting smaller towns rather than the same famous places.\"\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Infer word meaning from context: understand how phrases in a spoken answer develop and balance a view."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: how a strong answer is built

Strong Part 3 answers are built from small moves:
- an opinion, often softened (I''d say, I suppose)
- a limit (at least economically)
- an example (for instance, in my home city)
- a balancing point (then again, even if)
- a direct answer, then the reason (Probably not. It depends on ...)

WORKED EXAMPLE
"That''s a tricky question, but on the whole I''d say the advantages are greater"
She buys time (''That''s a tricky question''), then gives a balanced opinion (''on the whole I''d say'').

Now answer six questions about the transcript.' || art),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'9b85d22ec1d922d9ed151872e5b3ae85ccfe439250a918cae3185d93d5bd8560',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
 insert into private.ielts_learning_tasks(code,version,title,skill,purpose,instructions,success_description,taxonomy_version_id,pilot_student,questions,content,review_record,content_sha256,requires_review) values('bh-ielts-targeted-reading-r81-v1','0.1.0','Vocabulary V4 step 6 of 6: Mixed check','reading','independent_check','Read LEARN FIRST and the worked example. Then answer six new questions. Work on your own, without notes, a dictionary or help. Tell your teacher if anything interrupted you.','Use the right phrase for the job, the natural collocation, and a reply that is answered, explained and balanced.','ad250533-8582-4bc5-986b-32b0c9640a16','b30e9c28-96f1-4d34-83e9-9b28b4926f42','[{"id": "q1", "prompt": "Which phrase introduces a balancing point?", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  Looking back, ..."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  It''s a kind of ..."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Then again, ..."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  I''d highly recommend ..."}]}, {"id": "q2", "prompt": "The beach was absolutely ______; the water was crystal clear.", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  tricky"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  down-to-earth"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  bustling"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  stunning"}]}, {"id": "q3", "prompt": "Which reply softens the opinion most naturally?", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  It is definitely and totally about cost."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  I suppose it''s mainly a question of cost."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Cost."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  Everyone knows it is about cost."}]}, {"id": "q4", "prompt": "You cannot remember the word ''ladle''. You say ...", "accepted_answers": ["C"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  a ladling"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  a soup"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  the big spoon you use to serve soup"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  I don''t know this word"}]}, {"id": "q5", "prompt": "Looking ______, I think more people will work from home.", "accepted_answers": ["B"], "taxonomy_node_id": "6ac2c820-15a8-4318-8969-c1610e7180b8", "supporting_node_id": "22e5951f-eefd-4db0-9ea8-ce06c4b7127c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  back"}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  ahead"}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  forward"}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  after"}]}, {"id": "q6", "prompt": "Examiner: ''Would that be true everywhere?'' Which answer is best?", "accepted_answers": ["D"], "taxonomy_node_id": "0cba9b30-01e3-4504-b8e7-d207d731e4b4", "supporting_node_id": "2c90af36-6b23-4037-a9a8-b81e189c856c", "options": [{"value": "A", "label": "A  That is a very good question and I will answer it now."}, {"value": "B", "label": "B  Yes."}, {"value": "C", "label": "C  Everywhere, everywhere is the same."}, {"value": "D", "label": "D  Probably not. It depends on the place; in a big city it might work, whereas in a village it could be difficult."}]}]'::jsonb,'{"scope": "Targeted IELTS vocabulary exercise; not a full paper.", "suggested_minutes": 7, "mapping_scope": "Task-specific reviewed focus with canonical English registry references. Not an IELTS/English equivalence or a pooled Academic Profile claim.", "focus_code": "bh-ielts-vocabulary-targeted-focus-v1", "teacher_notes": "1 C, Then again: it adds the other side after you have given one view.\n2 D, stunning: extremely beautiful, like ''breathtaking''. ''Bustling'' is busy; ''down-to-earth'' describes people.\n3 B, ''I suppose ... mainly'' softens the opinion. The others are too strong or too short.\n4 C, Describe the thing and what you use it for.\n5 B, ahead: ''looking ahead'' = thinking about the future. ''Looking forward'' means feeling happy about something coming, which is different.\n6 D, A direct answer, then ''it depends on'' with a contrast (whereas) develops it well.\nRead each explanation, then use the word or phrase in a sentence of your own.", "focus": "Natural spoken vocabulary: phrase functions, collocations, repair strategies and developed replies."}'::jsonb || jsonb_build_object('passage', 'LEARN FIRST: the whole toolkit

- Jobs: buy time, soften, balance, rephrase, describe a missing word, reflect.
- Collocations: a bustling market, a stunning view, a down-to-earth person, highly recommend.
- Replies: answer + reason + example, natural and not memorised.
- Stuck? Describe the word, or ask politely for repetition.

WORKED EXAMPLE
''Looking ______, it was the right decision to move.''
Thinking about the past -> Looking back

Now answer six new questions on your own.'),'{"author": "Brains Heist AI-assisted original", "rights": "Original Brains Heist text; no third-party passages or questions copied.", "bible": "2.0.0", "human_review": "pending", "difficulty_comparability": "Not calibrated equivalent forms; no bands. Change is judged only by bh-practice-effect-v1 (provisional).", "source": "docs/ielts/practice/TARGETED_VOCABULARY_01.json 0.1.0"}'::jsonb,'32ac97be9bbc6338aec779135eaa8b0462f2419ce283f7cf10781699aba79b56',true) on conflict (code) do nothing;
end $steps$;
